---
import { RESUME, GITHUB, LINKEDIN, EMAIL } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="wrap about__grid">
    <h2 id="about-h" data-reveal>About</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I'm a computer science student at Carleton University (B.C.S. Honours, AI and Machine Learning stream), graduating in May 2028, and I want to spend my career on the code that decides how a game feels in your hands.</p>
      <p>I play Black Ops&nbsp;6 and Overwatch, and that's a big part of why I'm aiming at gameplay programming: movement, gunplay and hit registration are the systems I most want to build.</p>
      <p>My day job is testing other people's software. Since May 2026 I've been a QA automation developer at the Department of National Defence, on a C# framework that turns recorded interactions into Excel-driven Selenium tests. I built its debug mode: a failed run pauses, the tester fixes the step in the spreadsheet, and the run resumes from the last passing step. Before that, from January to April 2026, I was an IP network engineering intern at Nokia, writing Python and Tcl regression suites for protocol state machines. Both jobs left me with a habit you'll see across these projects: if a system matters, it gets an automated test.</p>
      <p class="about__contact">The fastest way to reach me is email: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. My <a href={RESUME}>résumé is a PDF</a>, my code is on <a href={GITHUB}>GitHub</a>, and my work history is on <a href={LINKEDIN}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about { padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .about__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr); gap: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem); align-items: start; }
  .about__contact { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.4; }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .about__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .about__contact a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
